home = f'''<section class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">Modding tools for TUNG</p><h1>Your game.<br><span>Your pace.</span></h1><p class="lede">Native mods and precise time controls, built for better practice. Install Wood once and manage your tools right inside TUNG.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="downloads.html">Download Wood <span>↓</span></a><a class="btn secondary" href="guides.html">Getting started ↗</a></div><p class="micro">Windows x64 · Version 2.1.1 · No Python installation needed</p></div>{demo}</section><div class="rail"><div><strong>Inside the game</strong>Native Unreal menus</div><div><strong>0.05× to 4×</strong>Adjust world speed</div><div><strong>One installer</strong>Runtime, launcher, uninstaller</div><div><strong>Made to extend</strong>Lua mods and settings</div></div><section class="section"><div class="sectionintro"><h2>A small toolkit.<br>A better practice session.</h2><p>Get straight to the tools you need, with a launcher for your library and a native menu for everything you use in game.</p></div><div class="tools"><div class="tool"><span class="tag">Included mod</span><h3>Time Warp</h3><p>Slow down a tricky section, repeat at normal speed, or move faster through practice. Presets, hotkeys, and an engine-confirmed speed readout keep control close.</p><a href="guides.html#time-warp">Explore the controls →</a></div><div class="tool"><span class="tag">Modding platform</span><h3>Wood Launcher</h3><p>Browse your mod library, enable native mods, and set up your next session. Lua extensions can add their own controls and persistent settings.</p><a href="developers.html">Build your first mod →</a></div></div></section><section class="section native">{native_svg}<div><p class="eyebrow">A part of your game</p><h2>A menu that belongs<br>inside TUNG.</h2><p>Press F10 or click Mods to open Wood’s native Unreal interface. Change settings, choose a preset, and return to your run.</p><p>The launcher stays available for setup and mod management. Your in-game controls use TUNG’s own widget system.</p><a class="textlink" href="about.html">How Wood works →</a></div></section><section class="section"><p class="eyebrow">From download to practice</p><h2>Ready in three steps.</h2><div class="steps"><div><div class="stepno">01 / DOWNLOAD</div><h3>Get the installer.</h3><p>A single Windows executable includes Wood and the pinned UE4SS runtime.</p></div><div><div class="stepno">02 / INSTALL</div><h3>Choose your TUNG folder.</h3><p>Setup detects Steam libraries and can configure the game’s launch options for you.</p></div><div><div class="stepno">03 / PLAY</div><h3>Launch. Press F10.</h3><p>Open the native mod menu, pick your speed, and start practicing.</p></div></div></section><section class="closing"><div><h2>Make the next attempt count.</h2><p>Start with Time Warp. Add your own tools as you go.</p></div><a class="btn" href="downloads.html">Get Wood ↓</a></section>'''

